This source code is published for ONE reason: so that anyone who runs River
Client, or is thinking about running it, can read exactly what it does and
confirm for themselves that it is not malware and is not doing anything behind
their back.

That is the whole point. It is not a grant of permission to use this code.

This is NOT open source in the OSI sense, and it is not free software.


WHAT YOU MAY DO

  1. Read, view and study this source code.
  2. Download or clone the repository for the purpose of reading it.
  3. Compile and run it locally, unmodified, purely to verify that the published
     River Client builds match this source.
  4. Quote short excerpts when reporting a bug, a security issue, or when
     discussing or reviewing River Client itself.


WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

  1. Use this code, in whole or in part, in any other project, product or
     service - free, paid, personal, public or private.
  2. Copy, reproduce, adapt, translate or create derivative works from it.
  3. Redistribute it, or distribute builds made from it.
  4. Reuse its code, assets, textures, icons, names or branding anywhere else.
  5. Publish a modified version of River Client, or a client based on it.
  6. Remove or alter this licence or the copyright notices.
  7. Use the "River" or "River Client" name, logo or branding for anything other
     than referring to this project.

If you want to do any of the above, ask first. Permission has to be given in
writing by the copyright holder, and without it the answer is no.


